---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProofStrip from '../components/ProofStrip.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'I’m relocating to Flower Mound. Who should I use?',
    a: 'Look for a local REALTOR® who can tour on your timeline, explain the trade-offs between Flower Mound pockets and nearby North DFW cities, and keep you informed from out of state. Diego Alvarado is a bilingual (English/Spanish) REALTOR® with Monument Realty, based in Flower Mound, who works with relocators through remote tours, honest pocket-by-pocket comparisons, and a clear next step after every call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I buy a home in Flower Mound without visiting first?',
    a: 'Many relocators start with live video tours and a narrowed shortlist, then fly in for a focused weekend. Diego can walk homes and streets on video, flag noise, drainage, and condition questions, and help you decide whether an in-person visit is needed before you write an offer.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should I choose the lake corridor or the airport side?',
    a: 'It depends on your commute and how you want to spend weekends. Flower Mound, Highland Village, and the lake towns lean toward trails, parks, and a residential pace; Coppell and Grapevine put you closer to DFW Airport and the SH 121 / SH 114 corridors. Drive or map your real peak-hour route before you decide.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I know which schools a home is zoned to?',
    a: 'Campus assignments are address-specific and can change. Verify the zone for the exact home with the district before you finalize — this site does not list school placements.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does a relocation purchase usually take?',
    a: 'Every move is different. Your loan approval, lease end date, job start, and how quickly you can tour all shape the timeline. Diego will map your dates backward from move-in day on the first call so you know what needs to happen first.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Relocating to Flower Mound & North DFW | Diego Alvarado REALTOR®"
  description="Relocating to Flower Mound or North DFW? Diego Alvarado, bilingual REALTOR® with Monument Realty, helps out-of-area buyers compare commutes, lake vs airport-side cities, timelines, and remote tours. Hablo Español."
>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container" style="max-width:42rem;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Relocating</p>
    <h1>Relocating to Flower Mound and North DFW</h1>
    <p>
      Moving from another city, state, or country means choosing a home — and a suburb — before
      you know the area well. Diego helps relocators compare Flower Mound and nearby North DFW
      cities honestly, tour remotely when you can’t be here, and keep the move on schedule.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Plan my move</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contacto/">Hablo Español</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container prose" style="max-width:42rem;">
    <h2>Who Diego is for relocators</h2>
    <p>
      Diego Alvarado is a REALTOR® with Monument Realty, based in Flower Mound. He is originally
      from Argentina and works in English and Spanish, so households can ask real questions
      without translation friction. Relocators get a local guide who explains trade-offs plainly,
      tours on your timeline, and sends a clear next step after every call or showing.
    </p>

    <h2>Lake corridor or airport side?</h2>
    <p>
      Most North DFW relocation shortlists split into two families. The <strong>Grapevine Lake
      corridor</strong> — <a href="/areas/flower-mound/">Flower Mound</a>,
      <a href="/areas/highland-village/">Highland Village</a>, and
      <a href="/areas/trophy-club/">Trophy Club</a> — leans toward parks, trails, and a residential
      pace. The <strong>airport side</strong> — <a href="/areas/coppell/">Coppell</a> and
      <a href="/areas/grapevine/">Grapevine</a> — puts you closer to DFW Airport and the SH 121 /
      SH 114 corridors. <a href="/areas/lewisville/">Lewisville</a> sits between them along I-35E.
      Every city has its own feel street by street, so treat this as a starting map, not a verdict.
    </p>
    <p>
      In Flower Mound, start with the <a href="/areas/flower-mound/subdivisions/">Flower Mound
      subdivisions guide</a> to see the approved list of communities, from lake-adjacent and golf
      neighborhoods to master-planned and estate pockets.
    </p>

    <h2>Commute first</h2>
    <p>
      Before you fall for a kitchen, map your real peak-hour drive to work, the airport, and the
      places you will visit every week. Two homes in the same city can sit on very different
      traffic paths. Diego can drive or map the route with you during a tour.
    </p>

    <h2>Your timeline</h2>
    <p>
      Lease end dates, job start dates, loan approval, and school calendars all pull on the same
      move. On the first call, Diego works backward from move-in day so you know what needs to
      happen first — pre-approval, a scouting trip, remote tours, or an offer window.
    </p>

    <h2>Remote tours</h2>
    <p>
      If you can’t be in North DFW yet, Diego can walk homes and streets with you on live video,
      point out condition, noise, and drainage questions, and help you narrow the list so any
      in-person trip is focused.
    </p>

    <h2>Schools: verify by address</h2>
    <p>
      Campus assignments are address-specific and can change. Verify the zone for the exact home
      with the district before you finalize. Taxes, HOA dues, and any MUD or special district also
      vary by address — confirm them for the specific property.
    </p>

    <h2>Relocation FAQs</h2>
    {faqs.map((f) => (
      <>
        <h3>{f.q}</h3>
        <p>{f.a}</p>
      </>
    ))}

    <h2>Next step</h2>
    <p>
      For the general buying process, see <a href="/buyers/">buyers</a>. Ready to talk about your
      move? Call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>, start at <a href="/contact/">/contact/</a>,
      or use <a href="/contacto/">Hablo Español → /contacto/</a> if Spanish fits your household better.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-actions" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Plan my move</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contacto/">Hablo Español</a>
    </p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section-alt" style="padding-top:2rem;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:42rem;">
      <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
        <p class="eyebrow">Client proof</p>
        <h2>What clients say</h2>
      </div>
      <ProofStrip />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
